  },
  "armedMicrophoneDeniedLinux": "The system does not let Woodshed Player use the microphone, so «Armed» is off again. Check in the sound settings of the system that the input device may be used, then switch it on again.",
  "@armedMicrophoneDeniedLinux": {
    "description": "#162"
  },
  "helpRecordingBodyDesktop": "“Record” at the top right starts and stops a recording through the microphone (the default input device of the system). The recording is saved losslessly as FLAC and appears in the library as a new track, named after date and time. Without an input device there is no “Record”. If Windows does not allow the microphone, switch it on in Settings › Privacy & security › Microphone, also for desktop apps.\n\nArmed: in Practice and Metronome, the switch “Armed” records from the microphone by itself. As soon as the level rises above the threshold, a recording starts, 1 second early; after a pause of the set length it ends. Space plays or pauses as usual and also ends a running recording. Then “Armed” goes off; to keep it armed for the next recording, switch off “Switch off after a recording” in its settings. Each recording lands in the library in the folder Recordings › date. The arrow beside the switch sets threshold, pause and whether it goes off after a recording. While “Armed” is on, “Record” is locked.",
  "@helpRecordingBodyDesktop": {
    "description": "#162"
  }
}
